<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila approves 3 bln Europeso issue by EBRD.</title>
<headline>Manila approves 3 bln Europeso issue by EBRD.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Monetary Board said on Friday it has approved a proposal from the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) to issue one-year Europeso notes worth 3.0 billion pesos.</p>
<p>Central Bank Governor Gabriel Singson said in a statement EBRD would be the third supranational authorised to float Europeso instruments.</p>
<p>The first two were the International Finance Corp and the World Bank which launched this week 2.6 billion pesos and 3.0 billion pesos worth of five-year Europeso bonds respectively.</p>
</text>
